# === Rule 11/12: a Lie group / root system declares its root-system data ==== #

ex:ecLieStructureComplete a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/lie-structure-complete.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:LieGroup declaring math:hasRootSystem, whose math:RootSystem declares its math:cartanMatrix, math:weylGroup, and math:rootSystemRank, and whose math:WeylGroup carries its math:AlgebraicStructure frame and is anchored through math:automorphismGroupOf, satisfies math:LieStructureShape, math:RootSystemShape, math:AutomorphismGroupShape, and math:AlgebraicStructureShape and validates with no findings (a rank-2 A₂ system, not the E8 fingerprint, so the E8 value gate stays inert)." .

ex:ecLieMissingRootSystem a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/lie-group-missing-root-system.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example omits math:hasRootSystem on a math:LieGroup (sh:minCount 1 on math:LieStructureShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:IncompleteLieStructure)." .

# === Rule 12b: an automorphism group is anchored to the structure it is symmetry of #

ex:ecAutomorphismGroupAnchored a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/automorphism-group-anchored.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:AutomorphismGroup declaring math:automorphismGroupOf (the structure whose symmetries it collects) alongside its math:AlgebraicStructure frame satisfies math:AutomorphismGroupShape and math:AlgebraicStructureShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecAutomorphismGroupUnanchored a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/automorphism-group-unanchored.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example omits math:automorphismGroupOf on a math:AutomorphismGroup (sh:minCount 1 on math:AutomorphismGroupShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:UnanchoredAutomorphismGroup). It carries the full math:AlgebraicStructure frame so the structure gate is satisfied, isolating the anchoring violation." .

# === Rule 12c: a root system claiming the E8 fingerprint declares the true Weyl order #

ex:ecE8WeylCanonical a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/e8-weyl-canonical.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:RootSystem with the E8 fingerprint (240 roots, rank 8) whose math:weylGroup declares math:groupOrder 696729600 — the true order of W(E8) — satisfies math:E8WeylOrderShape (and math:RootSystemShape, math:AutomorphismGroupShape, math:AlgebraicStructureShape) and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecE8WrongWeylOrder a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/e8-wrong-weyl-order.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example carries the E8 fingerprint (240 roots, rank 8) but declares a math:weylGroup of math:groupOrder 696729599 instead of 696729600 (the SPARQL constraint of math:E8WeylOrderShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:WrongE8WeylOrder). The root system and Weyl group are otherwise complete, isolating the wrong-value violation — the flagship invariant is checked by value." .

# === Rule 13: a homomorphic-encryption scheme declares op + hardness + noise = #

ex:ecHeSchemeComplete a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/he-scheme-complete.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:HomomorphicEncryptionScheme declaring math:homomorphicOver, math:securityAssumption, math:noiseModel, and — as a math:RingHomomorphism — math:preservedOperation and a resource-valued math:preservationLaw satisfies math:HomomorphicEncryptionSchemeShape, math:HomomorphismShape, and math:PreservationLawShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecHeMissingNoiseModel a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/he-scheme-missing-noise-model.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example omits math:noiseModel on a math:HomomorphicEncryptionScheme (sh:minCount 1 on math:HomomorphicEncryptionSchemeShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:UnderspecifiedEncryptionScheme). It declares math:preservedOperation, math:homomorphicOver, math:preservationLaw, and math:securityAssumption so the homomorphism and hardness gates are satisfied, isolating the noise-model violation." .

# === Rule 14: a ring declares the distributivity law tying its two operations = #

ex:ecRingDistributive a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/ring-distributive.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:Ring declaring math:satisfiesDistributivity (the distributivity law) alongside its carrier, operations, and an axiom satisfies math:RingDistributivityShape and math:AlgebraicStructureShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecRingMissingDistributivity a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/ring-missing-distributivity.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example omits math:satisfiesDistributivity on a math:Ring (sh:minCount 1 on math:RingDistributivityShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:NonDistributiveRing). It declares its carrier, both operations, and an axiom so the general math:AlgebraicStructureShape is satisfied, isolating the distributivity violation." .

