# === Residual meaning is an observation, not a property ===================== #

ex:ecResidualMeaningObserved a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/residual-meaning-observed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:ResidualInterpretationClaim naming its gmeow:vantage, gmeow:observedFeature, and gmeow:observationResult satisfies math:ResidualInterpretationClaimShape and validates with no findings — the meaning is held from a standpoint, not stamped on the vector." .

ex:ecResidualMeaningUngrounded a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/residual-meaning-ungrounded.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example names the observed feature and result but omits the gmeow:vantage (sh:minCount 1 on math:ResidualInterpretationClaimShape) — a meaning without a standpoint is a property, not an observation — so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:ResidualMeaningAsProperty)." .

