# === Tensor computation graph reuses the expression AST ===================== #

ex:ecTensorGraphFramed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/tensor-graph-framed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:TensorComputationGraph declaring a math:computationNode that is a well-formed math:ApplicationExpression over indexed math:ArgumentSlot operands, with a math:WeightTensor in a declared math:ParameterSpace, satisfies math:TensorComputationGraphShape, math:WeightTensorShape, and the inherited argument-slot shapes, and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecTensorNodeDuplicateSlotIndex a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/tensor-node-duplicate-slot-index.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A tensor computation node reuses the expression AST wholesale, so two math:argumentSlot cells sharing math:slotIndex 0 trip the inherited math:SlotIndexUniquenessShape SPARQL constraint exactly as any application/binder would; validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:MalformedArgumentSlot)." .

ex:ecApplicationTwoOperators a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/application-two-operators.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MaxCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:ApplicationExpression carrying two math:operator values (math:matrixProduct and math:tensorContraction) is ambiguous which operator it applies; its two math:argumentSlot cells are well-formed with distinct indexes, so it trips only math:ApplicationExpressionShape (sh:maxCount 1 on math:operator). Validation MUST emit shacl.MaxCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:ApplicationOperatorCardinality)." .

ex:ecTensorGraphNoNode a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/tensor-graph-no-node.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:TensorComputationGraph declaring no math:computationNode has an empty forward pass and no operator to apply; it names its architecture but omits the required node, so it trips only math:TensorComputationGraphShape (sh:minCount 1 on math:computationNode). Validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:MalformedTensorComputationGraph)." .

ex:ecWeightTensorNoParameterSpace a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/weight-tensor-no-parameter-space.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example names the layer the weight parameterizes but omits the math:ParameterSpace it lives in (sh:minCount 1 on math:WeightTensorShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:UnframedWeightTensor)." .

# === Bridges: ingest-run grounding (parseSource + schema/plan witness) ======= #

ex:ecIngestRunGrounded a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/ingest-run-grounded.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:IngestRun that retains its source through math:parseSource and carries the process-layer in-band witness through logic:instantiatesSchema and logic:instantiatesPlan satisfies math:IngestRunShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecIngestRunUngrounded a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/ingest-run-ungrounded.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example carries the process-layer witness (logic:instantiatesSchema / logic:instantiatesPlan) but omits math:parseSource (sh:minCount 1 on math:IngestRunShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:UngroundedIngestRun)." .

# math:UnliftableIngest is a NATIVE Rust gate (crates/validate structural_lint, keyed on a
# math:parseSource-retaining math:IngestRun that produces no gmeow:wasGeneratedBy codomain),
# NOT a SHACL shape, so it has no example-conformance cell here — the conformance harness only
# asserts SHACL findings. Its slice-resident counter-example
# (tests/counter-examples/ingest-run-unliftable.ttl — a produced-nothing run that still passes
# math:IngestRunShape) is exercised by the native lint test
# unliftable_ingest_fires_when_run_produces_no_codomain, distinguishing the produced-nothing case
# from the source-dropping math:UngroundedIngestRun SHACL grounding shape above.

